{"id":"mahabharata-5-179","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":179,"title":"एकोनाशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 179 · The battle begins at Kurukshetra","summary":{"en":"Parashurama and Bhishma meet at Kurukshetra, Bhishma on his chariot with his mother Ganga trying in vain to dissuade him. Parashurama appears with a chariot and armour of his own creation, and Bhishma first salutes his teacher before the fight.","kn":"ಪರಶುರಾಮ ಭೀಷ್ಮರು ಕುರುಕ್ಷೇತ್ರದಲ್ಲಿ ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ರಥದಲ್ಲಿದ್ದ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ತಾಯಿ ಗಂಗೆ ತಡೆಯಲು ವ್ಯರ್ಥವಾಗಿ ಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಪರಶುರಾಮನು ತಾನೇ ಸೃಷ್ಟಿಸಿದ ರಥ ಕವಚಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕಾಣಿಸಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುದ್ಧಕ್ಕೆ ಮುನ್ನ ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಗುರುವಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"परशुराम और भीष्म कुरुक्षेत्र में आमने-सामने होते हैं, भीष्म रथ पर हैं और उनकी माता गंगा उन्हें रोकने का व्यर्थ प्रयास करती हैं। परशुराम स्वयं रचे रथ और कवच के साथ प्रकट होते हैं, और युद्ध से पहले भीष्म गुरु को प्रणाम करते हैं।","te":"పరశురాముడు, భీష్ముడు కురుక్షేత్రంలో తలపడతారు; రథంపై ఉన్న భీష్ముని తల్లి గంగ వారించడానికి వృథాగా ప్రయత్నిస్తుంది. పరశురాముడు తాను సృష్టించిన రథం, కవచంతో కనిపిస్తాడు; యుద్ధానికి ముందు భీష్ముడు గురువుకు నమస్కరిస్తాడు.","ta":"பரஶுராமரும் பீஷ்மரும் குருக்ஷேத்திரத்தில் சந்திக்கிறார்கள்; தேரில் இருக்கும் பீஷ்மரை அவர் தாய் கங்கை தடுக்க வீணாக முயல்கிறாள். பரஶுராமர் தாமே படைத்த தேருடனும் கவசத்துடனும் தோன்ற, போருக்கு முன் பீஷ்மர் ஆசிரியரை வணங்குகிறார்.","ml":"കുരുക്ഷേത്രത്തിൽ പരശുരാമനും ഭീഷ്മരും കണ്ടുമുട്ടുന്നു; തേരിലിരിക്കുന്ന ഭീഷ്മരെ, പിന്മാറ്റാൻ വൃഥാ ശ്രമിക്കുന്ന അമ്മ ഗംഗ പിന്തുടരുന്നു. പരശുരാമൻ തന്റെതന്നെ സൃഷ്ടിയായ തേരും കവചവും അണിഞ്ഞ് പ്രത്യക്ഷനാകുന്നു; പോരാട്ടത്തിനുമുമ്പ് ഭീഷ്മർ ആദ്യം തന്റെ ഗുരുവിനെ വണങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.179; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो मामब्रवीद्रामः प्रहसन्निव भारत ।\nदिष्ट्या भीष्म मया सार्धं योद्धुमिच्छसि संगरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, as if laughing, said to me, Bharata: It is good luck, Bhishma, that you want to fight me in battle."}},{"n":2,"text":"अयं गच्छामि कौरव्य कुरुक्षेत्रं त्वया सह ।\nभाषितं तत्करिष्यामि तत्रागच्छेः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"I go now to Kurukshetra with you, Kaurava; I will do as I said; come there, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र त्वां निहतं माता मया शरशताचितम् ।\nजाह्नवी पश्यतां भीष्म गृध्रकङ्कबडाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, slain by me and covered with hundreds of arrows, Mother Jahnavi will see you, Bhishma, eaten by vultures, herons and ravens."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृपणं त्वामभिप्रेक्ष्य सिद्धचारणसेविता ।\nमया विनिहतं देवी रोदतामद्य पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The goddess served by siddhas and charanas will see you pitiful, struck down by me, and weep today, king."}},{"n":5,"text":"अतदर्हा महाभागा भगीरथसुता नदी ।\nया त्वामजीजनन्मन्दं युद्धकामुकमातुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great and blessed river, Bhagiratha's daughter, did not deserve to have given birth to you, a fool, a lover of war, and sick."}},{"n":6,"text":"एहि गच्छ मया भीष्म युद्धमद्यैव वर्तताम् ।\nगृहाण सर्वं कौरव्य रथादि भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Come, go, Bhishma, let the battle take place today; take all your equipment, chariot and the rest, Kaurava, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":7,"text":"इति ब्रुवाणं तमहं रामं परपुरंजयम् ।\nप्रणम्य शिरसा राजन्नेवमस्त्वित्यथाब्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Rama, conqueror of enemy cities, said this, I bowed my head and said \"So be it,\" king."}},{"n":8,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ययौ रामः कुरुक्षेत्रं युयुत्सया ।\nप्रविश्य नगरं चाहं सत्यवत्यै न्यवेदयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus, Rama went to Kurukshetra, eager to fight; and I entered the city and told Satyavati."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः कृतस्वस्त्ययनो मात्रा प्रत्यभिनन्दितः ।\nद्विजातीन्वाच्य पुण्याहं स्वस्ति चैव महाद्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having had the blessing rites performed and been blessed by my mother, I had the twice-born recite the auspicious words of well-being, radiant one."}},{"n":10,"text":"रथमास्थाय रुचिरं राजतं पाण्डुरैर्हयैः ।\nसूपस्करं स्वधिष्ठानं वैयाघ्रपरिवारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I mounted a splendid chariot adorned with silver, drawn by white horses, well furnished and well built, covered with tiger skin."}},{"n":11,"text":"उपपन्नं महाशस्त्रैः सर्वोपकरणान्वितम् ।\nतत्कुलीनेन वीरेण हयशास्त्रविदा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was equipped with great weapons and every requirement, driven by a hero of that stock who knew the science of horses."}},{"n":12,"text":"युक्तं सूतेन शिष्टेन बहुशो दृष्टकर्मणा ।\nदंशितः पाण्डुरेणाहं कवचेन वपुष्मता ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was driven by a disciplined charioteer who had often been seen at his work; I was armored in a bright white coat of mail."}},{"n":13,"text":"पाण्डुरं कार्मुकं गृह्य प्रायां भरतसत्तम ।\nपाण्डुरेणातपत्रेण ध्रियमाणेन मूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking a white bow, I set out, best of Bharatas, with a white umbrella held over my head."}},{"n":14,"text":"पाण्डुरैश्चामरैश्चापि वीज्यमानो नराधिप ।\nशुक्लवासाः सितोष्णीषः सर्वशुक्लविभूषणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fanned with white chowries, king, dressed in white, with a white turban and all ornaments white,"}},{"n":15,"text":"स्तूयमानो जयाशीर्भिर्निष्क्रम्य गजसाह्वयात् ।\nकुरुक्षेत्रं रणक्षेत्रमुपायां भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Praised with blessings of victory, I left Hastinapura and came to Kurukshetra, the field of battle, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":16,"text":"ते हयाश्चोदितास्तेन सूतेन परमाहवे ।\nअवहन्मां भृशं राजन्मनोमारुतरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged on by that charioteer in the great fight, those horses, swift as mind and wind, bore me on at great speed, king."}},{"n":17,"text":"गत्वाहं तत्कुरुक्षेत्रं स च रामः प्रतापवान् ।\nयुद्धाय सहसा राजन्पराक्रान्तौ परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I reached Kurukshetra, and the mighty Rama too; we both eagerly came forward for battle against one another."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः संदर्शनेऽतिष्ठं रामस्यातितपस्विनः ।\nप्रगृह्य शङ्खप्रवरं ततः प्राधममुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I stood in sight of Rama, the great ascetic, took up my excellent conch and blew it loudly."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततस्तत्र द्विजा राजंस्तापसाश्च वनौकसः ।\nअपश्यन्त रणं दिव्यं देवाः सर्षिगणास्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brahmins there, ascetics and forest dwellers, and the gods with groups of sages, watched that divine battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो दिव्यानि माल्यानि प्रादुरासन्मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nवादित्राणि च दिव्यानि मेघवृन्दानि चैव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then divine garlands appeared again and again, and divine instruments and masses of clouds."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततस्ते तापसाः सर्वे भार्गवस्यानुयायिनः ।\nप्रेक्षकाः समपद्यन्त परिवार्य रणाजिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all those ascetics, followers of the Bhargava, became spectators, standing around the battlefield."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो मामब्रवीद्देवी सर्वभूतहितैषिणी ।\nमाता स्वरूपिणी राजन्किमिदं ते चिकीर्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the goddess, in her own form, my mother, who wishes the good of all beings, said to me, king: What is this that you intend?"}},{"n":23,"text":"गत्वाहं जामदग्न्यं तं प्रयाचिष्ये कुरूद्वह ।\nभीष्मेण सह मा योत्सीः शिष्येणेति पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will go to Jamadagni's son and beg him, again and again, \"Do not fight Bhishma, your pupil.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"मा मैवं पुत्र निर्बन्धं कुरु विप्रेण पार्थिव ।\nजामदग्न्येन समरे योद्धुमित्यवभर्त्सयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"She rebuked me: Do not, my son, so insist on fighting the Brahmin Jamadagni's son in battle, king."}},{"n":25,"text":"किं न वै क्षत्रियहरो हरतुल्यपराक्रमः ।\nविदितः पुत्र रामस्ते यतस्त्वं योद्धुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do you not know, my son, that Rama, destroyer of Kshatriyas, has a valor like Hara's, since you want to fight him?"}},{"n":26,"text":"ततोऽहमब्रुवं देवीमभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nसर्वं तद्भरतश्रेष्ठ यथावृत्तं स्वयंवरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I saluted the goddess with folded hands and told her everything that had happened at the self-choice, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":27,"text":"यथा च रामो राजेन्द्र मया पूर्वं प्रसादितः ।\nकाशिराजसुतायाश्च यथा कामः पुरातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told her how Rama had once been appeased by me, and how the Kashi princess's wish was of old, king of kings."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः सा राममभ्येत्य जननी मे महानदी ।\nमदर्थं तमृषिं देवी क्षमयामास भार्गवम् ।\nभीष्मेण सह मा योत्सीः शिष्येणेति वचोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then my mother, the great river, goddess, went to Rama and begged that sage, the Bhargava, for my sake, saying: Do not fight Bhishma, your pupil."}},{"n":29,"text":"स च तामाह याचन्तीं भीष्ममेव निवर्तय ।\nन हि मे कुरुते काममित्यहं तमुपागमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to her as she begged: Turn Bhishma back himself; for he does not do my wish. So I went up to him."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो गङ्गा सुतस्नेहाद्भीष्मं पुनरुपागमत् ।\nन चास्याः सोऽकरोद्वाक्यं क्रोधपर्याकुलेक्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ganga, out of love for her son, came again to Bhishma, but he, his eyes disturbed with anger, did not obey her."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथादृश्यत धर्मात्मा भृगुश्रेष्ठो महातपाः ।\nआह्वयामास च पुनर्युद्धाय द्विजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the righteous Bhrigu's best, of great austerity, the best of the twice-born, appeared and challenged me again to battle."}}]}]}